codemap 9
tour gate
kind flow
author ai
group tooling
note cargo xtask gate: the single yes/no for whether the working copy is acceptable. Every rule the repo holds is a step here, run in a fixed order, cheapest first, stopping at the first failure; nothing is done until it is green. It exists so an agent cannot finish or commit code shaped any other way than the one the rules allow: the Stop hook runs it before a session may end, the pre-tool hook runs it before any commit, and each failing step reports in the words of the check that failed, so the agent learns the rule at the moment it breaks it instead of from a document. The steps: rustfmt, archlint, the crate graph, the API lock, clippy with warnings denied, the unit tests (archlint's fixtures among them), codemap check, the feature coverage test, and with --full the CLI scenarios. The GUI scenarios need a display and stay out. Every run records its result in the gate state, which the hooks read.

