note Reads the workspace members from the root manifest and each member's [dependencies] keys, and reports every dependency that is not in arch.rs DEPENDENCIES for that package. The message names the file the graph lives in, so an intended dependency is added there as an edge, in the same change, rather than routed around. Layering is held by the compiler (a crate can only use what it depends on) and this check holds the dependency list itself.

